share (IS_COMP_EPS_ADJUSTED), joined on fiscal_year; the median over the closed fiscal years carrying both with adjusted EPS above zero."}}}, "px_last": {"value": 238.93, "mnemonic": "PX_LAST", "vintage": "2026-09-30T08:39:13Z"}, "ratio_to_px_last": 3.319391834378506, "band": [0.33, 3.0], "band_basis": {"low": {"value": 0.33, "calibration": "uncalibrated", "basis": "AMGT_CORPUS round 6 h-2 @6d18367755: the 0.33-0.5 bin is EMPTY over 97 measured block keys and the only name below 0.33 is refused for a different cause, so this floor has never decided a case in the measured population."}, "high": {"value": 3.0, "calibration": "measured", "basis": "AMGT_CORPUS round 6 h-2 @6d18367755: over 97 measured block keys two names sit inside the ceiling between 2.5 and 3.0 and one sits just outside at 3.043, so this ceiling discriminates real cases."}}, "label": "Opal's historical-multiple reference"}, "upside": {"status": "ABSENT", "reason": "methodology to be discussed with Andrew"}, "downside": {"status": "ABSENT", "reason": "methodology to be discussed with Andrew"}}, "reason": null, "generated_at": "2026-09-30T11:36Z", "team_cases": {"base": {"status": "SERVED", "table": {"EPS": {"2026E": "24.37", "2027E": "27.48", "2028E": "31.44", "2029E": "35.33", "2030E": "38.60"}, "Multiple": {"2026E": "9.0x", "2027E": "9.0x", "2028E": "9.0x", "2029E": "9.0x", "2030E": "9.0x"}, "Price": {"2026E": "233", "2027E": "247", "2028E": "283", "2029E": "318", "2030E": "347"}, "Return": {"2026E": "5.6%", "2027E": "12.0%", "2028E": "28.1%", "2029E": "43.9%", "2030E": "57.3%"}}, "citation": {"locator": 0, "passage": "2026E 2027E 2028E 2029E 2030E | EPS 24.37 27.48 31.44 35.33 38.60 | Multiple 9.0x 9.0x 9.0x 9.0x 9.0x | Price 233 247 283 318 347 | Return 5.6% 12.0% 28.1% 43.9% 57.3%", "report_id": "a89e0cd31b4919a5", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ADBE_US_Equity/a89e0cd31b4919a5/ADBE research pack 7_13_2026.pdf"}, "currency": null, "currency_basis": "not stated in the pack", "unit_as_written": null}, "upside": {"status": "SERVED", "table": {"EPS": {"2026E": "24.16", "2027E": "27.86", "2028E": "32.15", "2029E": "35.56", "2030E": "39.33"}, "Multiple": {"2026E": "16.0x", "2027E": "16.0x", "2028E": "16.0x", "2029E": "16.0x", "2030E": "16.0x"}, "Price": {"2026E": "416", "2027E": "446", "2028E": "514", "2029E": "569", "2030E": "629"}, "Return": {"2026E": "88.4%", "2027E": "101.8%", "2028E": "132.8%", "2029E": "157.5%", "2030E": "184.8%"}}, "citation": {"locator": 0, "passage": "2026E 2027E 2028E 2029E 2030E | EPS 24.16 27.86 32.15 35.56 39.33 | Multiple 16.0x 16.0x 16.0x 16.0x 16.0x | Price 416 446 514 569 629 | Return 88.4% 101.8% 132.8% 157.5% 184.8%", "report_id": "a89e0cd31b4919a5", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ADBE_US_Equity/a89e0cd31b4919a5/ADBE research pack 7_13_2026.pdf"}, "currency": null, "currency_basis": "not stated in the pack", "unit_as_written": null}, "downside": {"status": "SERVED", "table": {"EPS": {"2026E": "23.06", "2027E": "24.68", "2028E": "26.42", "2029E": "27.10", "2030E": "27.78"}, "Multiple": {"2026E": "6.0x", "2027E": "6.0x", "2028E": "6.0x", "2029E": "6.0x", "2030E": "6.0x"}, "Price": {"2026E": "143", "2027E": "148", "2028E": "159", "2029E": "163", "2030E": "167"}, "Return": {"2026E": "-35.2%", "2027E": "-33.0%", "2028E": "-28.2%", "2029E": "-26.4%", "2030E": "-24.6%"}}, "citation": {"locator": 0, "passage": "2026E 2027E 2028E 2029E 2030E | EPS 23.06 24.68 26.42 27.10 27.78 | Multiple 6.0x 6.0x 6.0x 6.0x 6.0x | Price 143 148 159 163 167 | Return -35.2% -33.0% -28.2% -26.4% -24.6%", "report_id": "a89e0cd31b4919a5", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ADBE_US_Equity/a89e0cd31b4919a5/ADBE research pack 7_13_2026.pdf"}, "currency": null, "currency_basis": "not stated in the pack", "unit_as_written": null}}, "line_names": {"PX_LAST": "Share price (last close)", "SALES_REV_TURN": "Revenue", "IS_OPER_INC": "Operating income", "OPER_MARGIN": "Operating margin", "CAPITAL_EXPEND": "Capital expenditure", "CF_FREE_CASH_FLOW": "Free cash flow", "CURRENT_EV_TO_T12M_EBITDA": "Enterprise value to trailing EBITDA", "REVENUE_PER_SH": "Revenue per share", "FREE_CASH_FLOW_YIELD": "Free cash flow yield", "FREE_CASH_FLOW_MARGIN": "Free cash flow margin", "PROF_MARGIN": "Net profit margin", "BS_CASH_NEAR_CASH_ITEM": "Cash and near-cash items", "BS_TOTAL_LIABILITIES": "Total liabilities", "IS_ADJUSTED_GROSS_PROFIT": "Adjusted gross profit", "IS_ADJUSTED_OPERATING_INCOME": "Adjusted operating income", "IS_COMP_EPS_ADJUSTED": "Adjusted earnings per share", "NET_INCOME": "Net income", "EQY_DPS": "Dividend per share, alternate definition", "IS_DIL_EPS_CONT_OPS": "Diluted EPS, continuing operations", "PX_TO_FREE_CASH_FLOW": "Price to free cash flow", "GROSS_MARGIN": "Gross margin", "EBITDA_TO_REVENUE": "EBITDA as a share of revenue", "RETURN_ON_CAP": "Return on capital", "RETURN_ON_INV_CAPITAL": "Return on invested capital", "RETURN_ON_TANGIBLE_ASSETS": "Return on tangible assets"}}, "dossier_fields": {"thesis_pillars": [{"citation": {"extract_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report-extract/security_key=ADBE_US_Equity/a89e0cd31b4919a5/extract.json", "locator": 1, "passage": "les growth, operating margins high and stable, strong free cash \nflow and a solid balance sheet. \n \nExpanding market opportunity with trends likely unfavorable to incumbents: AI is \ncollapsing the cost and skill barriers to content creation just as demand for content \nexpl", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ADBE_US_Equity/a89e0cd31b4919a5/ADBE research pack 7_13_2026.pdf"}, "pillar": "Expanding market opportunity with trends likely unfavorable to incumbents", "terms": ["Expanding market opportunity with trends likely unfavorable to incumbents", "cost"], "text": "AI is collapsing the cost and skill barriers to content creation just as demand for content explodes across every channel. But the industry trend within that opportunity is unfavorable to incumbents, because the same forces that grow the pie are commoditizing the tools, compressing seat counts, and inviting competitors in from every direction, leaving Adobe with a bigger TAM and a weaker claim on it. While Adobe sizes the market at nearly $300bn, third-party sources estimate it\u2019s closer to $100bn."}, {"citation": {"extract_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report-extract/security_key=ADBE_US_Equity/a89e0cd31b4919a5/extract.json", "locator": 1, "passage": " \nAdobe sizes the market at nearly $300bn, third-party sources estimate it\u2019s closer to \n$100bn.  \n \nEntrenched standard for creative professionals fighting various competitive threats: \nAdobe largely created the market and had a near-monopoly (90%+ share) for much of \nthe last 20 ye", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ADBE_US_Equity/a89e0cd31b4919a5/ADBE research pack 7_13_2026.pdf"}, "pillar": "Entrenched standard for creative professionals fighting various competitive threats", "terms": ["Entrenched standard for creative professionals fighting various competitive threats"], "text": "Adobelargelycreated the market and had a near-monopoly (90%+ share) for much of the last 20 years. They benefit from switching costs, a strong brand and scale advantages. Adobe is defended by workflow lock-in, file formats, enterprise integration and IP-safe AI. The last few generations of creators have been trained on Adobe tools in school, and many organizations have standardized on their products. The Adobe brand carries a trust premium that has arguably strengthened in the AI era as they offer clean training data and IP indemnification (commercially safe models are particularly valuable for large enterprise). While foundation models have lowered the barrier to scale, scale still matters for the integrated suite."}], "management": {"status": "SERVED", "value": "Management and capital allocation: CEO Shantanu Narayen joined Adobe in 1998 as VP and GM of engineering technology. He became president and COO in 2005 and CEO in 2007. Before Adobe, he held product development roles at Apple and Silicon Graphics and co-founded an early photo-sharing startup, Pictra. Earlier this year, he announced he would be stepping down as CEO as soon as the board finds a replacement (he will remain as chair of the board). The two internal frontrunners are presidents Anil Chakravarthy (Customer Experience Orchestration Business) and David Wadhwani (Creativity and Productivity Business). Anil has been with Adobe since 2020, joining from Informatica where he served as CEO. He also held leadership roles at Symantec and VeriSign prior to Informatica. David joined Adobe in 2005 through the acquisition of Macromedia where he was VP of developer products. In addition to Shantanu stepping down, CFO Dan Durn recently resigned to join Marvell (a fabless chip designer). He was previously CFO of GlobalFoundries and Applied Materials, so his return to semiconductors in the AI boom isn\u2019t entirely surprising. In addition to internal frontrunners, the board is evaluating external candidates for the CEO position as well. The cluster of turnover and change at the top comes at a time when Adobe is executing its biggest strategic pivot in history. On capital allocation, priorities include reinvesting back into the business, strategic tuck-in M&A and returning excess capital to shareholders through buybacks. While declining as a percent of total sales (currently high-teens), R&D remains a priority. They\u2019ve spent nearly $35bn in R&D on a cumulative basis over the last three decades. In the most recent deal, they paid $1.9bn for Semrush, a brand visibility platform positioned around generative engine optimization. While most other deals in recent years have been of this magnitude, they did attempt to acquire Figma in 2022 for $20bn. The deal was blocked by regulators, and Adobe was forced to pay a $1bn termination fee. Since the mid-1990s, they\u2019ve repurchased nearly $59bn in shares outstanding, with more than half of those buybacks in the last five years (or nearly 14% of total shares outstanding). The board recently announced a new share repurchase authorization for $25bn through the end of April 2030.", "citation": {"locator": 2, "passage": "Management and capital allocation: CEO Shantanu Narayen joined Adobe in 1998 as VP and GM of engineering technology. He became president and COO in 2005 and CEO in 2007. Before Adobe, he held product development roles at Apple and Silicon Graphics and co-founded an early photo-sharing startup, Pictr", "report_id": "a89e0cd31b4919a5", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ADBE_US_Equity/a89e0cd31b4919a5/ADBE research pack 7_13_2026.pdf"}}, "fund_of_record": {"status": "ABSENT", "value": null, "reason": "no report's RECOMMENDATION line names a fund token (IDVZ|PFOE|DIVZ)"}, "last_stated_position": {"status": "ABSENT", "value": null, "reason": "no report carries a non-empty RECOMMENDATION line"}}, "generated_at": "2026-09-30T11:36Z", "drafted_sections": [], "drafting_status": "ABSENT", "drafting_source": "none", "drafting_read_completed": true, "drafting_reason": "no drafted document at s3://opal-data-harvest/drafting/v1/ADBE_US_Equity.json: NoSuchKey: An error occurred (NoSuchKey) when calling the GetObject operation: The specified key does not exist.", "held_uncited_count": 0, "held_uncited_basis": "NOT_SERVED", "held_no_span_count": 0, "held_no_span_basis": "NOT_SERVED", "thesis_driver": null, "as_of_date": null, "thesis_driver_chart": {"status": "ABSENT", "reason": "no thesis_driver on a served D-1 document", "points": [], "points_count": 0}, "management": {"security_key": "ADBE_US_Equity", "management_status": "ABSENT", "absent_because": "NO_OBJECT